<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32702" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏphīon</span></b> ,
		ŏnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀφίων</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One of the giants</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 3,
			348</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the companions of Cadmus;</i> hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏphīŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Ophion;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> for <i>Theban</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ophionia caedes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of Pentheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Oedip. 483</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The father of Amycus</i>, <i>the
				Centaur;</i> hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏphīŏnĭdes</span></b> ,
				ae, m., <i>the son of
				Ophion</i>, <i>the Ophionide</i>, of Amycus,
				<i><span class="en">Ov.
				M. 12, 245</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
